284			<section>
285				<p>This is a well-structured, accessible HTML5 document demonstrating modern best practices for semantic markup and inclusive design.</p>
286				<p>
287					It uses semantic landmarks, a skip link for keyboard navigation,
288					and CSS that adapts to your light or dark mode preference.
289				</p>
290				<p>
291					Text and link colors meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes, type scales
292					with your browser's font size, and motion respects your system settings.
293				</p>
294			</section>
295	
296			<section aria-labelledby="features">
297				<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
298				<ul>
299					<li>Semantic HTML structure with proper landmarks</li>
300					<li>Keyboard accessible navigation and focus management</li>
301					<li>Dark mode support with custom color schemes</li>
302					<li>Responsive typography using modern CSS</li>
303					<li>Print-friendly styles for better readability</li>
304					<li>WCAG AA contrast compliance in all color modes</li>
305				</ul>
306			</section>
307	
308			<section aria-labelledby="examples">
309				<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>
310				<article class="card">
311					<h3>Component Cards</h3>
312					<p>Card components are useful for organizing related content. They include a subtle border and padding for visual separation.</p>
313					<a class="button" href="#resources">Learn more<span class="visually-hidden"> about accessibility resources</span></a>
314				</article>
315	
316				<article class="card">
317					<h3>Interactive Elements</h3>
318					<p>Buttons and links are fully accessible with clear focus states. The “Learn more” button above demonstrates smooth transitions and proper visual feedback.</p>
319					<p>Try using the Tab key to navigate through all interactive elements.</p>
320				</article>
321			</section>
322	
323			<section aria-labelledby="resources">
324				<h2 id="resources">Resources</h2>
325				<p>Want to learn more about web accessibility and semantic HTML? Check out these resources:</p>
326				<ul>
327					<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/">WCAG 2.2 Quick Reference</a></li>
328					<li><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/">HTML Living Standard</a></li>
329					<li><a href="https://www.a11y-101.com/">A11y 101</a></li>
330				</ul>
